meta {
  name: Transfer Work
  type: http
  seq: 20
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/{{activeUserId}}/work-transfer
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ownerAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "toUserId": "{{successorUserId}}"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("names the colleague and counts what moved", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.toUserId).to.equal(bru.getVar("successorUserId"));
    expect(body).to.have.property("toName");
    expect(body).to.have.property("tickets");
    expect(body).to.have.property("households");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /users/:userId/work-transfer

  Hand a person's **open** work to a named colleague (PAC-136) — the
  departing-employee case that used to need a hand-written migration. Works on
  an active **or an already-removed** person. Removing someone *and* handing
  their work over in one step is `DELETE /users/:userId` with `successorId`.

  **Module** — none (`@SkipModule`). **Permission** — `agency:work_transfer:write`
  + `agency:users:read`, granted per role (Agency Owner by default) — **and the
  role must be agency-wide**. A branch- or own-scoped holder is refused with
  `403` even with the permission (product owner, 2026-10-05).

  **No cross-branch transfers.** The successor must be in the departing
  person's branch, unless either of them has no branch (typically an owner).

  **Body** — `{ "toUserId": "<24-hex user id>" }`. Pick it from **List Transfer
  Candidates**, which applies the same rules.

  ## What moves
  Still-to-do work, plus the fields that mint the *next* piece of work:
  - Non-terminal service tickets (`assignedUserId` + `assignedRep`), each with a
    "Reassigned from X to Y." timeline note.
  - In-progress onboardings and renewal cycles (`assignedCsrId`) — so the next
    onboarding call and renewal tickets are created for the successor.
  - Households (`assignedCrmId`) and their deal mirror (`deals.assignedCrmId`).
  - Non-terminal leads (`producerId`), with a `lead_reassigned` activity each.
  - **Every outstanding audit responsibility** (product owner, 2026-10-05):
    open deal audits where the person is the user assignee or reviewer; open
    audits on their sales that nobody was assigned to; and every **unresolved**
    audit item on their sales (`producerId` + `producerName`). The successor can
    resolve them, and the Manager dashboard counts them against the successor.
    Role-owned audits stay with their role.
  - Live share links (`producerId`), so public URLs keep working.
  - Round-robin slots (`crmRotations.crmId`): taken over where the successor has
    no active slot for that producer, switched off otherwise — a pool is never
    doubled, and `activeForProducer` is never turned on.

  ## What never moves
  Attribution — `deals/quoteRecaps.producerId`, **resolved** audit items, `createdBy*`,
  `completedBy*`, timeline authors, activity actors — and `branchId`. Closed
  tickets, sold/lost leads, finished onboardings and passed audits stay put.

  Every touched `_id` is recorded in `workTransfers`.

  **Response `201`** — the preview's counts plus `{ fromUserId, toUserId, toName }`.

  **Errors**
  - `400` — `toUserId` is the same person, or malformed.
  - `403` — missing permission, or the caller's role is not agency-wide.
  - `404` — either user is not in this agency (or is a platform admin).
  - `409` — the successor is not an active user, or holds none of the
    departing person's roles (a producer's book goes to a producer, a CSR's to
    a CSR; anyone is allowed only if the departing person holds no role), or
    works in a different branch.

  ## ⚠ Side effect on the demo tenant
  This really moves the demo user's open work to `successorUserId`. Restore with
  `npm run api:seed:demo:dev -- --fresh` if you need the demo data intact.
}
